[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Human escalation is most reliable when it is triggered by clear, task-relevant conditions: the customer explicitly asks for a human, the required resolution involves a policy exception, or the agent cannot make meaningful progress. These conditions directly reflect a need for human judgment or assistance, unlike sentiment thresholds, fixed retry counts, or rigid category mappings.

