[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Reports should distinguish conclusions that are well established from those that remain contested, while preserving each source’s stated uncertainty, methodology, and evidentiary character. This communicates genuine disagreement without arbitrarily selecting a result, flattening uncertainty into a single number, or obscuring useful context with generic hedging.

