[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Explicit structured claim-to-source mappings preserve citation provenance through synthesis and enable the combined report to retain the exact supporting sources for every conclusion. Attempting to infer attribution afterward from transcripts, semantic similarity, or text prefixes is less reliable than carrying provenance as first-class structured metadata.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
