[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }When a backend failure prevents execution of an otherwise eligible refund, the agent should explain the available billing information and eligibility result, clearly disclose that the system issue prevents immediate processing, and provide a follow-up option such as escalation or a later retry. This preserves transparency and advances the customer’s resolution without falsely confirming that an uncompleted refund has been processed.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
